      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, when evaluating such cases, it's crucial to prioritize accurate patient history and a thorough physical examination. Document any \"atypical\" features that are not characteristic of standard melanocytic nevi. It might be useful to consider a broader range of potential diagnoses and use the most specific ICD-10 code available that captures the nuances of these atypical presentations. If the situation remains ambiguous, consulting a specialist or using a multidisciplinary approach might provide additional clarity. Finally, remember that obtaining the ICD-10 code with the highest specificity enhances the accuracy and thoroughness of clinical documentation.",
